First row: (cosθ-1)a + sinθ b=0. Use cosθ-1=-2 sin^2 θ/2, sinθ=2 sin θ/2 cos θ/2. Then -2 sin^2 a + 2 sin cos b=0 => b = tan(θ/2) a. Normalize a=cos θ/2, b=sin θ/2. Yes.

