\[
x_k=\frac1{y_k}-1=\frac{B_k-A_k}{A_k},
\]
so the sum \(m+n\) for \(x_k\) is exactly \(B_k\).

One can show inductively that
\[
B_{k+1}=\frac{B_k^2}{3},
\]
with \(B_1=36\). Hence
\[
B_k=2^{2^k}\cdot 3^{2^{k-1}+1}.
